<title>USA: SEC chair urges ABA delegates to end pay-to-play.</title>
<headline>SEC chair urges ABA delegates to end pay-to-play.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>SEC Chairman Arthur Levitt urged more than 500 American Bar Association delegates meeting here Wednesday to &quot;send pay-to-play down the road demise.&quot;</p>
<p>Levitt spoke as ABA delegates opened debate on whether to adopt a draft resolution approved by key association panels on the campaign finance issue. The resolution condemns pay-to-play by lawyers, urges bar groups to adopt rules discouraging the practice and calls for a task force to study whether to adopt a tough ban on pay-to-play already approved by the New York City bar.</p>
</text>
